          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**Yes. One component-issue event for manufacturing order MO-25-09-1070 was created 75 minutes after September entered Pending Close. Its recorded `POSTED` status is inconsistent with Oracle’s documented treatment.**\n\n### Audit finding\n\n| Item | Recorded value |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | `WO-2025-09-004` |\n| Operation / product | Racine DeKoven — Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost event | `CE-250904-0004` — `INPUT` (component issue) |\n| Source transaction | **`TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070`** |\n| Amount | **USD $284,763.42** (`28,476,342` cents) |\n| Cost period | `Sep-25` — `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** |\n| Exact event-created time | **`2025-09-30T19:15:00`** |\n| Time after Pending Close | **75 minutes** — 1 hour 15 minutes |\n| Recorded accounting status | **`POSTED`** |\n\n**Calculation:** `19:15:00 − 18:00:00 = 4,500 seconds ÷ 60 = 75 minutes`.\n\nThe timestamps above are reproduced exactly as recorded; the source does not specify a time-zone offset.\n\n### Policy conclusion\n\nThe supplied Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B documentation states that newly created transactions falling in the Pending Close period or an earlier period **will not be staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting** until the period is closed or reopened. Pre-existing transactions can continue processing, as can the specified exceptions: revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments.\n\nThis event was a **new component issue dated September 30**, created after the cutoff—not an identified exception. Its `POSTED` status therefore **does not conform to the documented Pending Close treatment**; it should have been held from staging and processing.\n\n**Sources:** `state.db` tables `work_orders`, `cost_periods`, and `work_order_cost_events`; supplied Oracle 26B guide, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225.\n\nThe review was read-only; no database records were changed. The report was submitted and verified, and the audit result with provenance was saved to `/cache/work/worker_85c0bb4450b2/audit-report.json`.",
